placing a shard (both master logic & on the nodes)"},{"id":7704422592,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAAe_f88AAAAByzgowA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/labels/Team:Distributed%20Coordination%20(obsolete)","name":"Team:Distributed Coordination (obsolete)","color":"fef2c0","default":false,"description":"Meta label for Distributed Coordination team. Obsolete. Please do not use."}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-01-13T23:47:13Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T04:05:27Z","closed_at":"2026-01-19T04:05:27Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I believe this is a bug introduced in 9.0. When the source index is deleted, the ResizeAllocationDecider throws on `null` index metadata due to the usage of [projectFor](https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/blob/f0349f836bd7d2ca5ce22b7ce5010b6f3c471797/server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/cluster/routing/allocation/decider/ResizeAllocationDecider.java#L43). But the code is mean to handle `null` indexMetadata as indicate by the null check right after the line. Indeed, [the version in 8.19](https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/blob/cc9a0b805e3ff31e1da20a4f38b4d7dba51412ff/server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/cluster/routing/allocation/decider/ResizeAllocationDecider.java#L42-L45) handles `null` properly. \n\nThrowing exception on `null` can break desired balance computation and effectively stops the allocation process.  We should fix it by handling deleted source index properly. ","closed_by":{"login":"elasticsearchmachine","id":58790826,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NzkwODI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58790826?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elasticsearchmachine","html_url":"https://github.com/elasticsearchmachine","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elasticsearchmachine/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elasticsearchmachine/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elasticsearchmachine/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elasticsearchmachine/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elasticsearchmachine/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elasticsearchmachine/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elasticsearchmachine/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elasticsearchmachine/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elasticsearchmachine/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/140630/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/140630/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}